<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Rosheim</h1><p class="st-meta">1303 CE – 1679 CE (approx.) · capital Rosheim</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the smallest Alsatian Decapolis cities, a wine town known for its Romanesque church of Saints Peter and Paul.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rosheim, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a> west of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-strasbourg">Strasbourg</a>, was an imperial possession under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>. The town was walled in the 13th century and its rights as a free imperial city were confirmed around 1303. In 1354 it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a>, the alliance of ten Alsatian imperial cities under the imperial bailiff at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-haguenau">Haguenau</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> governed this small community of vintners, farmers and craftsmen. Its church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-saints-peter-and-paul-rosheim">Saints Peter and Paul</a>, built in the 12th century of yellow sandstone, is one of the finest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanesque-architecture">Romanesque</a> buildings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, and the town also preserves a stone house of the same age. Rosheim remained Catholic.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The town suffered heavily in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. After 1648 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a> came under French protection, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen">Treaty of Nijmegen</a> of 1679 confirmed its incorporation into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>. It is now a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bas-rhin">Bas-Rhin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1303 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.63%;width:7.48%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1303 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rosheim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alsatian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rosheim</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1491&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-rosheim" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Rosheim on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4853 483 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Rosheim lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5173 739L5918 1245"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5918 1245h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5173 739h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5173 739h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rosheim. <a href="/atlas?year=1491&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-rosheim">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

